  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Environmental Transformation of Agrifood in Myanmar (PRET Myanmar)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;The overall objective is that the Myanmar agri-food sector transitions to a low-carbon, resource-efficient and circular economy business model, whilst promoting more sustainable value chains and products, contributing to the recovery of local economies.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The specific objectives are the following:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- Analogue forest and agroforestry production systems and improved logistics increase the productivity of tea producers, reduce on-farm environmental impacts and contribute to climate adaptation and mitigation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- The environmental impacts of tea processing are mitigated through reduced energy and water intensity, low-carbon energy, innovative and sustainable packaging and improved waste management.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- Tea sector transformation provides reproducible, profitable business models for climate and biodiversity-positive production and reduced plastic use which stimulates similar transitions in the wider Myanmar agri-food sector.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
